
  ── A server I will rent ───────────────────────────────────── step 3 of 4 ──

    A user for your agents

    Agents should not run as root. Log in once as root, and make a user with
    your key:
      ssh root@203.0.113.10
      adduser --disabled-password --gecos "" dev
      usermod -aG sudo dev
      echo "dev ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL" > /etc/sudoers.d/dev
      install -d -m 700 -o dev -g dev /home/dev/.ssh
      install -m 600 -o dev -g dev ~/.ssh/authorized_keys /home/dev/.ssh/
    …

    User         dev

    ✕ ssh         dev@203.0.113.10

    ✕ Cannot log in to dev@203.0.113.10 with ssh yet: Permission denied
      (publickey).
    → ssh dev@203.0.113.10   (run it yourself to see what it asks)

